    {
      "path": "tests/helpers/callback-fin-packages.mjs",
      "currentSha256": "6e062c3f22a8fd8375938f3bf07f6d6266beaf670f1cad1662f46ecd231cc4e9",
      "previousSha256": "5883b0ab3544beb591fb5eb36ebcba06a7dcc4b1a5709e332edb95871df86b7a",
      "edits": [
        {
          "start": 6576,
          "previous": "",
          "current": "/** Each package's source, exports and closure arities; the browser acceptance reuses them unchanged. */\nexport const callbackFinCases = Object.freeze({\n\tscalar: { source: scalarSource, names: [\"three\", \"five\", \"closure\", \"emptyInput\", \"twice\", \"emptyArray\", \"emptyOption\", \"nested\"], arities: { \"OnboardingSmall.closure\": 1, \"OnboardingSmall.emptyInput\": 1 } }\n\t, nominal: { source: nominalSource, names: [\"packet\", \"digits\", \"tree\", \"choice\", \"packetClosure\", \"scalar\"], arities: { \"OnboardingSmall.packetClosure\": 1 } }\n});\n\n"
        },
        {
          "start": 8035,
          "previous": "\tfor(const [profile, source, check, names, arities] of [\n\t\t[\"scalar\", scalarSource, scalarCheck, [\"three\", \"five\", \"closure\", \"emptyInput\", \"twice\", \"emptyArray\", \"emptyOption\", \"nested\"], { \"OnboardingSmall.closure\": 1, \"OnboardingSmall.emptyInput\": 1 }]\n\t\t, [\"nominal\", nominalSource, nominalCheck, [\"packet\", \"digits\", \"tree\", \"choice\", \"packetClosure\", \"scalar\"], { \"OnboardingSmall.packetClosure\": 1 }]\n\t]) {\n",
          "current": "\tfor(const [profile, check] of [[\"scalar\", scalarCheck], [\"nominal\", nominalCheck]])\n\t{\n\t\tconst { source, names, arities } = callbackFinCases[profile];\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/lean/existing-package.md",
      "currentSha256": "1eba16b5ff9d3524b7de0348913dd146c1397a6c6eb2435f26853a650d2797ef",
      "previousSha256": "0ac19e5cec7f88ad75e28f512fb6c7f40f843b157327aeecc23a709c9ad5f6a6",
      "edits": [
        {
          "start": 44876,
          "previous": "",
          "current": "The [ordinary-source browser callback run](../evidence/browser-callback-fin-20261008/receipt.json) executes fourteen exports in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit pages, React production/strict effects and dedicated workers. Each of the twelve contexts records 409 checks and 894 rejected calls. These cover host replies, returned closures, nested containers and nominal or recursive fields, including `Fin 0`, recovery after rejection and closure disposal. The checks distinguish public JavaScript rejection from compiled-adapter rejection and verify the installed WebAssembly bytes served by the page. Author sources and build staging are removed before offline installation. This run does not measure dispatch or establish reviewed-browser or native host-reply acceptance.\n\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/evidence/refinement-closure-audit-20261007.md",
      "currentSha256": "1e44837fdc7abb8f82e55d922a75347baaf352165d675569b20a930209c08f9d",
      "previousSha256": "85bfd2e28845833f6b725830cee007100b62646c6dd5b4abc878c95bac882aff",
      "edits": [
        {
          "start": 2731,
          "previous": "| Fin callback positions | Ordinary-source Node JavaScript/TypeScript; C/C++ safe native directions, with 297 C checks and 283 C++ checks. | The [C/C++ archive](native-fin-callbacks-20261008/receipt.json) preserves the original source-free installed run and separate C public-entry, checked-adapter and source-body counters. | Native host-produced refined replies remain refused. C++ dispatch was not measured; other native hosts, reviewed callbacks and browser callbacks need separate acceptance. The local C/C++ run uses glibc 2.36 and does not establish release-floor acceptance. |\n",
          "current": "| Fin callback positions | Ordinary-source Node JavaScript/TypeScript; C/C++ safe native directions, with 297 C checks and 283 C++ checks. The [browser archive](browser-callback-fin-20261008/receipt.json) records twelve Chromium/Firefox/WebKit page, React and worker contexts, each with 409 checks and 894 rejections. | The [C/C++ archive](native-fin-callbacks-20261008/receipt.json) preserves the original source-free installed run and separate C public-entry, checked-adapter and source-body counters. Browser reports preserve exact installed/deployed WebAssembly identities, source removal and lifecycle checks; dispatch is unmeasured. | Promote only these observed browser positions. Native host-produced refined replies remain refused. Reviewed callback reports and other native hosts remain separate. The local C/C++ run uses glibc 2.36 and does not establish release-floor acceptance. |\n"
        }
      ]
    },
